From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shuuri-labs <61762328+shuuri-labs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:36:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: skip identity colour LUTs in the composite
 shader

With SDR content on an SDR panel and no night mode, gain or gamut remap,
the shaper and 3D LUTs gamescope builds are an identity transform, yet the
composite shader still samples both per pixel. On a GPU that composites
every frame that is the larger half of the pass. Detect the identity grids
on the CPU when the LUTs are rebuilt and leave them unbound for the shader;
the DRM plane path keeps its blobs.

Two Steam defaults kept the LUT from ever being identity. It drives the
SDR gamut wideness to 0.5; where scanout cannot be colour managed that
remap only reaches composited frames, so a game looks different the moment
an upscaler or overlay forces a composite. Keep SDR content in the native
gamut on such backends. It also sets a virtual white that is D65 quantised
differently from the 709 constant; a virtual white within 0.001 xy of the
display's is treated as no override. Night mode and the gains still
rebuild a real LUT when set.

The color_mgmt_skip_identity_luts and color_mgmt_native_gamut_without_plane_cm
convars (default on) restore the old paths for A/B.
